+# CONTRACT — CLI Time Tracker
+
+Public API exported from `src/index.ts`.
+
+## Behaviors
+
+- [ ] `start(name)` begins a named timer → test: an entry with that name and `end === null` exists
+- [ ] `start` with empty/whitespace name throws → test: `expect(() => t.start('')).toThrow()`
+- [ ] Starting while one is running auto-stops the previous → test: previous entry gets a non-null `end`, only one running entry remains
+- [ ] `stop()` ends the running timer → test: running entry's `end` becomes non-null
+- [ ] `stop()` with nothing running throws → test: `expect(() => t.stop()).toThrow()`
+- [ ] Entries capture name, start, end(null if running) → test: shape assertions
+- [ ] Persistence: data saved to configurable JSON path, survives reload → test: new tracker on same path reads prior entries
+- [ ] Parent dirs + file auto-created → test: nested non-existent dir path works
+- [ ] `getEntries()` returns all entries → test: count matches
+- [ ] `getEntriesInRange(from, to)` filters by start time → test: only entries whose start ∈ [from,to]
+- [ ] `summary()` returns total ms per task name, summed → test: two entries same name sum
+- [ ] Running tasks use current time in summary → test: running entry contributes (now - start)
+- [ ] Unicode/emoji task names work → test: round-trip through persistence + summary
+
+## Done
+
+`npm run build` clean, `npm run lint` clean, `npm test` all pass.
